<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>8.1.5: Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m02094</md:content-id>
    <md:title>8.1.5: Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>81a3e7e0-0766-46de-b43b-611f1c0c5872</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section>
      <para>Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
      <section class="check-understanding">
        <exercise data-content-id="ddd8d7a4-d23a-4d5a-b35d-49e504aa12a4" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Use the following scenario to answer questions 1 – 3.</para>
            <para>A water balloon is launched by a catapult into the air. The water balloon is launched from 4 feet above the ground, with an initial vertical velocity of 40 feet per second.</para>
            <para>The function \(h(t)=-16t^2 + 40t + 4\) models the height of the water balloon over the ground, in feet, \(t\) seconds after launch.</para>
            <para>
              <figure>
                <media alt="A DOWNWARD PARABOLA. X-AXIS LABEL IS TIME IN SECONDS AND Y-AXIS LABEL IS HEIGHT IN FEET. THE GRAPH PASSES THROUGH THE POINTS (0, 4), (0.5, 20), (1, 28), (1.5, 28), (2, 20), AND (2.5, 4).">
                  <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_09_03_10_01.jpg"/>
                </media>
              </figure>
            </para>
            <para>What is the height of the water balloon 1 second after launch?</para>
            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>18 feet</para>
            <para>22 feet</para>
            <para>28 feet</para>
            <para>34 feet</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct!</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 8.1.1.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is 28 feet. </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise data-content-id="1be11c84-cac7-4c2b-a1b7-9167d49e00a8" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Will the water balloon still be in the air 2 seconds after the launch?</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct!</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 8.1.1.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is yes. </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise data-content-id="a533105e-d0af-4da7-967b-ccef854cc82c" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Using the graph, estimate when the water balloon hit the ground.</para>
            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>1.2 seconds</para>
            <para>1.8 seconds</para>
            <para>2.1 seconds</para>
            <para>2.6 seconds</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct!</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 8.1.1.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is approximately 2.6 seconds. </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise data-content-id="4422f95e-f1f8-48d2-bf0d-cfade1823c86" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Use the following scenario to answer questions 4 – 5.</para>
            <para>
              <quote>Suppose you want to frame a different picture that measures 12 inches by 9 inches. The frame is created from 46 square inches of framing material. The frame must be uniform in width, and all of the framing material must be used.</quote>
            </para>
            <para>Which of the following is true about the situation described?</para>
            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>The perimeter of the picture is 40 inches.</para>
            <para>The perimeter of the framed picture is 42 inches.</para>
            <para>The area of the framed picture is 148 square inches.</para>
            <para>The perimeter of the framed picture is greater than 42 inches.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct!</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 8.1.2.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is the perimeter of the framed picture is greater than 42 inches. </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise data-content-id="1ae10f49-546a-48b8-bb26-ddbd7b9a1c3d" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>What is the total area of the framed picture?</para>
            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>46 square inches</para>
            <para>108 square inches</para>
            <para>154 square inches</para>
            <para>176 square inches</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct!</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 8.1.2.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is 154 square inches. </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise data-content-id="6b5eaf55-8eee-4a1a-a8ee-c3934e06334e" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Use the following scenario to answer questions 6 – 8.</para>
            <para>
              <quote>Suppose you want to frame a different picture that measures 9 inches by 8 inches. The frame is created from 38 square inches of framing material. The frame must be uniform in width, and all of the framing material must be used. Let \(x\) represent the thickness of the frame.</quote>
            </para>
            <para>What is the total area of the framed picture?</para>
            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>34 square inches</para>
            <para>72 square inches</para>
            <para>110 square inches</para>
            <para>134 square inches</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct!</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 8.1.3.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is 110 square inches. </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise data-content-id="6a449a14-2cd1-4fc4-bbfd-f71f176ea2bf" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Write an equation to represent the relationship between the measurements of the picture and of the frame and the area of the framed picture.</para>
            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>\(x^2 + 34x = 38\)</para>
            <para>\(4x^2 + 34x = 72\)</para>
            <para>\(x^2 + 34x + 72 = 110\)</para>
            <para>\(4x^2 + 34x + 72 = 110\)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct!</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 8.1.3.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is \(4x^2 + 34x + 72 = 110\). </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise data-content-id="39bb92af-ed5e-43a7-a333-cfa5c679ca6f" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>What does the solution to the equation in the previous question represent in this situation?</para>
            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>The solution represents the area of the framing material that should be used. </para>
            <para>The solution represents the thickness of the frame when all of the framing material is used.</para>
            <para>The solution represents the perimeter of the frame when all of the framing material is used.</para>
            <para>The solution represents the total area of the framed picture.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct!</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 8.1.3.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is the thickness of the frame when all of the framing material is used. </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise data-content-id="a4e79ad6-377a-4762-bfed-389be7b9a423" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Use the following scenario to answer questions 9 – 10.</para>
            <para>
              <quote>A framed picture has a total area \(y\), in square inches. The thickness of the frame is represented by \(x\), in inches. The equation \(y = (2x + 5)(2x + 7)\) relates these two variables.</quote>
            </para>
            <para>What are the width and length of the picture without the frame?</para>
            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>2 inches and 2 inches</para>
            <para>2 inches and 5 inches</para>
            <para>2 inches and 7 inches</para>
            <para>5 inches and 7 inches</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct!</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 8.1.4.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is 5 inches and 7 inches. </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise data-content-id="abad243c-0cd5-40c2-84e1-bb24cf570b68" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Which of the following represents the area of the frame?</para>
            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>\(y − 35\)</para>
            <para>\(x + y\)</para>
            <para>\(x + 35\)</para>
            <para>35</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! </para>
            <para> Try again. Revisit activity 8.1.4.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is \(y - 35\). </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      </section>
    </section>
  </content>
</document>
